{
  "name": "Kiln",
  "tagline": "Pottery glaze colours: raku smoke, tenmoku iron, celadon jade.",
  "story": "Kiln takes its colours from glazed pottery rather than from neon: copper lustre for keywords, cobalt blue for strings, celadon green for numbers, ash-glaze straw for types and Jun-ware purple for parameters. Raku is the smoke-blackened clay just pulled from the fire, Tenmoku is the brown-black iron glaze of a tea bowl, and Celadon is the pale jade glaze for daylight. The grounds are matte and low in saturation like fired clay, so only the glaze colours stand out; body text is AAA and every syntax colour, comments included, is at least AA.",
